<p>Peru’s National Elections Board confirmed that Keiko Fujimori and Roberto Sánchez will compete in a June 7 presidential runoff after neither candidate won more than half of valid votes in the first round. Fujimori, a 50-year-old congresswoman from Fuerza Popular and daughter of former President Alberto Fujimori, led with 2.8 million votes, or 17.19%, while Sánchez, a Juntos por el Perú candidate and former foreign trade minister under Pedro Castillo, received 2.015 million votes, or 12.03%. The official proclamation followed a prolonged count from the April 12 vote. Rafael López Aliaga finished third with about 11.9%, narrowly behind Sánchez, and Peru has had eight presidents since 2016.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/byJb3lcPDnvqgk1gnEjWWwJ3DYkcZiOEK16J1oSASyiyugkCPPg6IV1vOR1Qk_qAtuBRQWz1GEkpbIG052i_pvF9P4OlVhjovvO3w6JIHFOn0vXfGmpnZ011fhvyy6mEZ20oPfmP93eXTQTioiustfECeETrUZbFyMAytCOVret2NzE81vcBsuxNOLmxumZ6ilSP2wtwWKIlFCU' alt='Keiko Fujimori, the leader of the Popular Force Party, at a campaign rally last month in Lima, Peru.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Narrow margin: Sánchez beat López Aliaga for second place by 21,209 votes, according to the official count cited by Diario Libre.</li><li>Election flaws: Peru’s top electoral authority pledged to correct voting “flaws” before the runoff and announced an expert committee including national and international specialists to help supervise it.</li><li>Crime focus: Both runoff candidates advanced from a 35-candidate field after campaigning on promises to address rising crime, a top concern for Peruvians.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>National Elections Board: JNE President Roberto Burneo said the proclamation closed an administrative step by Peru’s highest electoral authority after the official count. (<a href='https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/internacional/america-latina/2026/05/17/jurado-nacional-de-elecciones-peruano-reafirma-y-oficializa-segunda-vuelta-entre-fujimori-y-sanchez.shtml'>BioBioChile</a>)</li><li>Renovación Popular: López Aliaga’s right-wing party said it would file a challenge after its candidate missed the runoff, according to BioBioChile’s account of Burneo’s remarks. (<a href='https://www.biobiochile.cl/noticias/internacional/america-latina/2026/05/17/jurado-nacional-de-elecciones-peruano-reafirma-y-oficializa-segunda-vuelta-entre-fujimori-y-sanchez.shtml'>BioBioChile</a>)</li><li>European Union election observation mission: The EU observation mission noted serious deficiencies in the first-round vote but still gave the election its full approval, Diario Libre reported. (<a href='https://www.diariolibre.com/actualidad/nacional/2026/05/17/autoridad-electoral-oficializa-balotaje-fujimori-y-sanchez-en-peru/3536404'>Diario Libre</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/perus-fujimori-and-sanchez-to-meet-in-june-7-presidential-runoff'>Peru&#x27;s Fujimori and Sánchez to meet in June 7 presidential runoff</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/05/17/left-wing-candidate-roberto-sanchez-advances-to-presidential-runoff-in-peru_6753533_4.html'>Left-wing candidate Roberto Sanchez advances to presidential runoff in Peru</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/peru-electoral-body-pledges-to-fix-voting-flaws-ahead-of-june-presidential-runoff'>Peru electoral body pledges to fix voting &#x27;flaws&#x27; ahead of June presidential runoff</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/perus-electoral-board-confirms-june-7-presidential-runoff-133050906'>Peru&#x27;s electoral board confirms June 7 presidential runoff with Fujimori and Sánchez</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/17/world/americas/peru-runoff-election.html'>Runoff in Peru Offers Two Starkly Differing Visions for the Nation</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/5/17/peruvia